---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HostBio from '../components/HostBio.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Why Wreck the Narrative exists: a gospel-first show on a John 10:10 spine. The lie in our own hearts first, then in the culture, then what Jesus says.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <span class="kicker">About the show</span>
      <h1>They say sin isn't real and Jesus isn't needed. <em>Both are lies.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Wreck the Narrative is a gospel show first. It talks about culture and politics, but only to get back to what Jesus says.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Why this show exists</h2>
      <p>There's one master narrative underneath all the others: <b>"Sin isn't real. And Jesus isn't needed."</b> Every other lie the show takes on grows out of that one.</p>
      <p>We work from the inside out. Cultural and political lies only stick because we've already believed smaller lies about ourselves. So we start with the heart — then the culture.</p>

      <h2>The John 10:10 spine</h2>
      <p>Every episode runs on one verse: <b>"The thief comes only to steal and kill and destroy. I came that they may have life and have it abundantly."</b> <span style="color:var(--steel);">(John 10:10, ESV)</span></p>
      <p>The flow is always the same: name the lie &rarr; show how it hits <b>our own lives</b> &rarr; show how it shows up in <b>culture</b> &rarr; show how the gospel wrecks both.</p>

      <h2>Three lanes</h2>
      <p>Every episode is filed under one lane. All three run on the same John 10:10 spine.</p>
      <div class="lane-cards">
        <div class="lane-card"><h3>The Heart</h3><p>The lies we believe about ourselves, sin and God — not enough, shame, going back to sin.</p></div>
        <div class="lane-card"><h3>The Home</h3><p>Men, family, the church, everyday faithfulness — and what you're willing to lose for Christ.</p></div>
        <div class="lane-card"><h3>The Public Square</h3><p>How a Christian thinks about government, money, voting and neighbor.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h2>What this show is — and isn't</h2>
      <p><b>It is:</b> gospel-first, honest, sourced. John works through his own struggles out loud, on purpose.</p>
      <p><b>It isn't:</b> a rage show, a party mouthpiece, or self-help with Jesus stickers. Politics is a tool, not the point — God doesn't care who wins an election the way we do; He cares what leaders stand for and the results of their decisions.</p>

      <h2>How we handle truth</h2>
      <p>We only call something a lie if it's provably false and documented. Opinion gets labeled as opinion. Sources are listed on every episode page.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        <b>Need help?</b> If an episode stirs up something heavy, talk to your pastor or a trusted friend — and get professional help when you need it.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <HostBio panel={true} />
</BaseLayout>
